sub1:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-bailleul-allometric-cranial-sutures> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-bailleul-allometric-cranial-sutures-overall> .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-bailleul-allometric-cranial-sutures-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Miura et al. (2009) & Jaslow (1990) cranial suture fractal interdigitation and Kuramoto-Sivashinsky osteogenic instability — MorphoEval overall 92.2/100" ;
        dcterms:date "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
        dcterms:description "Pass 2 post-remediation evaluation of `2020-bailleul-allometric-cranial-sutures.py` (92.4/100, up from 57.3/100 in Pass 1; +35.1 overall). The remediated script integrates the damped Kuramoto-Sivashinsky / KPZ osteogenic front PDE via pseudo-spectral integrating-factor / ETDRK2 time-stepping coupled to 2D bidirectional overhanging normal-front propagation and a Twist1/BMP4 mesenchymal cleft phase field across all 5 canonical regimes: neonatal infant flat suture (`D_f = 1.0315`, `SII = 1.0732`), adult sagittal fractal suture (`D_f = 1.3484`, `SII = 2.9181`), adult lambdoid hyper-interdigitated suture (`D_f = 1.3756`, `SII = 3.3431`), surgical mechanical unloading null control (`D_f = 1.0000`, `SII = 1.0000`), and FGFR2 Apert craniosynostosis fusion (`D_f = 1.0000`, `SII = 1.0000`), alongside Jaslow (1990) bending energy absorption scaling (`2.687x` amplification in lambdoid vs fused suture) and automated CV trace extraction (`D_f = 1.2847`, `SII = 2.6791`, log-log correlation `r = 0.9949`) on `human_sagittal_suture_specimen.jpg`, backed by 3 machine-checked Lean 4 theorems in `Loop_020_allometric_cranial_sutures.lean`. Overall 92.2/100 (faithfulness 91.9, reproducibility 93.0); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 317bc3c; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.4.2, scipy 1.17.0, matplotlib 3.10.8, Pillow 12.1.1. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 94, Morphological realism / specimen match 90, Parameter expressivity 92, Morphometric validation 92, Source and data traceability 93, Code-to-model traceability 93, Reproducibility package 93. Output judged: docs/media/allometric_cranial_sutures_comparison.png: rendered output of 2020-bailleul-allometric-cranial-sutures.py at 317bc3c, image/png, 1121609 B, 2227×1782 px, artifact_sha256 a9db7edbea67db2b4950a5be983f2eb6d96310a6e86b3135d5babf4b038114b2 (sha256 a9db7edbea67db2b4950a5be983f2eb6d96310a6e86b3135d5babf4b038114b2), spec_fingerprint 53dc68ef4189bb186f820ba54b5a160dfe42da44326e82b66ab860cc7d2ad00e. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 53dc68ef4189bb186f820ba54b5a160dfe42da44326e82b66ab860cc7d2ad00e; artifact_sha256: a9db7edbea67db2b4950a5be983f2eb6d96310a6e86b3135d5babf4b038114b2; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/allometric_cranial_sutures/allometric_cranial_sutures_reference.json=dbb634957fb6941d..., datasets/allometric_cranial_sutures/human_sagittal_suture_specimen.jpg=b3c411a6a4713770..., datasets/allometric_cranial_sutures/paper_citations.bib=bffc86bbbd2dd3d6..., datasets/allometric_cranial_sutures/scout_manifest.json=226c072307597439...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-19-allometric-cranial-sutures-audit. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Miura et al. (2009) PNAS 106:11218-11223 fourth-order Kuramoto-Sivashinsky / KPZ osteogenic front instability dh/dt = -alpha*d^2h/dx^2 - beta*d^4h/dx^4 + (v_0/2)*(dh/dx)^2 + eta(x,t) generating self-affine fractal cranial suture interdigitation (D_f ~ 1.30-1.45) and collapse to a flat line under surgical mechanical unloading | Jaslow (1990) J. Biomech. 23:313-321 monotonic enhancement of cranial suture bending and impact energy absorption with Suture Interdigitation Index SII = L_arc / L_chord | Khonsari et al. (2013) Proc. R. Soc. B 280:20122670 & Zollikofer & Weissmann (2011) J. Anat. 219:100-114 bidirectional normal-front overhang and FGFR2 craniosynostosis fusion; reconstructed_in_script: Pseudo-spectral integrating-factor / ETDRK2 Kuramoto-Sivashinsky + KPZ nonlinear normal-growth solver coupled to 2D bidirectional overhanging front propagation and mesenchymal cleft phase field across 5 developmental/pathological regimes and a 15x15 (alpha, beta) morphospace | Automated CV calvarial segmentation, sagittal suture midline cleft extraction, SII (2.6791), and 5-scale dyadic box-counting fractal dimension (D_f = 1.2847, log-log r = 0.9964) on human_sagittal_suture_specimen.jpg; transfer_boundary: 1D/2D overhanging osteogenic suture front geometry (x(s), y(s)), box-counting dimension D_f, Suture Interdigitation Index SII, and Jaslow bending energy ratio compared against superior-view human calvarial sagittal suture morphology; does_not_claim: 3D trabecular diploe micro-CT finite-element fracture mechanics or single-cell scRNA-seq trajectories of Twist1+/Runx2+ suture stem cells." ;
        dcterms:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: Couple spatially heterogeneous masticatory finite-element strain tensors across the coronal, sagittal, and lambdoid sutures on a 3D skull mesh.",
            "remediation needed: Extend the 2D overhanging calvarial suture solver to full 3D ectocranial-to-endocranial cortical plate thickness where endocranial sutures remain simpler than ectocranial traces." ;
        pk:hasScore "0.922"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Gemini 4 Argon (primary) + Claude Sonnet 5.5 High (independent second assessor)" ;
        dcterms:identifier "gemini-4-argon" ;
        prov:actedOnBehalfOf orcid:0009-0007-4948-9192 ;
        foaf:homepage <https://deepmind.google> .
}

